    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39356" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">psythĭus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">psĭthĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψύθιος</span> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψιθ</span>-), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>psythian</i>, a
			designation of a species of vine: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 4, 269</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Col. 3, 2, 24</span></i>.—Called also
			simply <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">psythĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f., <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 2, 93</span></i>; and in
			plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">psythiae (sc. uvae),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 4, 9, 38</span></i>
			.—<i>Neutr. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">psythĭum</span></b> ,
				ii, <i>a kind of raisin - wine</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				14, 9, 11, § 80</span></i>.</div>
